  "handling": {
    "lookup_order": [
      "Check mappings for an exact legacy block ID.",
      "If absent, check ambiguous.",
      "If neither exists, preserve the namespaced identifier unchanged."
    ],
    "ambiguous_policy": "Do not choose among multiple modern blocks. Preserve or report the legacy aggregate statistic because the old metadata variant is not encoded in the statistic key.",
    "namespace_policy": "Map only the path after minecraft:. Preserve non-minecraft namespaces unchanged.",
    "statistic_context": "Use this mapping only for the suffix of stat.mineBlock.<block-id>."
  },
  "notes": [
    "Minecraft 1.12.2 often stored several block variants under one block ID and distinguished them by metadata. Statistics keyed by block ID aggregate those variants, so a one-to-many split cannot be reconstructed from the key alone.",
    "This mapping is for statistic keys, not block-state or world-chunk conversion.",
    "The direct mappings are a conservative set of legacy identifier renames and should be checked against the software's actual 1.12.2 StatList keys.",
    "For a legacy block that has one modern equivalent but appears in ambiguous for historical context, the ambiguous entry takes precedence unless the implementation explicitly treats a single possible_targets entry as a safe alias."
  ],
  "references": [
    "https://minecraft.wiki/w/Java_Edition_Flattening",
    "https://minecraft.wiki/w/Java_Edition_pre-flattening_data_values"
  ]
